## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/crystalnoise.html
- Summary (EN): Generates sharp, angular Worley-type noise in image coordinates by combining two randomly offset Worley noises. Suited to rock patterns, chipping and similar hard-edged detail.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère un bruit de Worley anguleux en coordonnées image, adapté aux roches et aux éclats.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets output size and metadata", "pos: optional UV layer replacing pixel image coordinates as the noise source", "time: optional layer giving a per-pixel time value"]

- Key parameters: ["Primary Metric: Euclidean, Manhattan or Chebyshev distance", "Jitter and Element Size: grid point randomness and base feature size in image coordinates; Element Scale per axis with Per-Component Controls", "Secondary, Secondary Metric, Secondary Jitter and Element Size: configure the second Worley noise", "Amplitude, Center, Noise Contrast: scale, offset and contrast of the raw noise", "Tile Size: repeat period for seamless tiling", "Flatten Faces: keeps faces flat instead of bulging", "3D Noise group (Animate, Pulse Length, Time Scale, Time Offset, Loop Length): time as a third dimension", "Post Processing (Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum): applied in that order"]

- Caveats: ["Values can fall below 0 or above 1; add a Clamp COP to enforce range.", "Jitter above 1 can cause artifacts.", "Complement assumes values between 0 and 1.", "Noise Contrast (inside the noise) differs from the post-processing Contrast.", "With Tile Size on, Element Size and similar values are rounded or clamped to stay tileable.", "For pure 3D noise use Crystal Noise 3D or Fractal Noise 3D."]

